Soft wrap: text wraps to the width its box is given, as on a web page.

Upstream's v1 line model breaks a run only on '\n', so an app has to know its
widths and wrap text itself with OP wrapText. With `Ui::set_soft_wrap(true)`
the layout does it in the same solve, the way a browser does:

- A text leaf is shaped once per character (`Fonts::wrap_units`). Its measure
  function counts the rows the run takes at the width Taffy offers, by the
  greedy rules of OP wrapText (`text::soft_wrap`), and answers that width and
  the rows' height. Its min-content width is its widest word.
- Taffy sizes a column item's flex basis with its unclamped cross size
  (`w-full` beside `max-w-[240px]`), so the measure clamps the offered width
  to the node's own min and max width first, as CSS does.
- Readback records where each row starts (`Node::soft_breaks`,
  `Ui::node_soft_breaks`), and paint draws those rows, dropping the spaces a
  row hangs. Node text is unchanged.

It is off by default, so upstream layouts and goldens do not change.

